From: Ali Zain <alizain@zainiumdynamics.tech>
Subject: [PATCH] nftables.service: ProtectSystem=strict

ProtectSystem=full makes systemd bind /usr read-only for the service and
fails when /usr does not exist, as on Zainium. strict protects the whole
tree from / instead, which is stricter and works without /usr.
---
diff --git a/tools/nftables.service.in b/tools/nftables.service.in
index 2ac7e6f..bd66536 100644
--- a/tools/nftables.service.in
+++ b/tools/nftables.service.in
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ ConditionPathExists=@pkgsysconfdir@/rules/main.nft
 Type=oneshot
 RemainAfterExit=yes
 StandardInput=null
-ProtectSystem=full
+ProtectSystem=strict
 ProtectHome=true
 ExecStart=@sbindir@/nft 'flush ruleset; include "@pkgsysconfdir@/rules/main.nft"'
 ExecReload=@sbindir@/nft 'flush ruleset; include "@pkgsysconfdir@/rules/main.nft"'
